From 92270bf81e3a3a1f420fe383a2eb3d2cada412b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Milan Patel <patelmm79@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:38:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(doctor): stop re-snapshotting already-migrated auth
 sources (#9)

Repeated doctor invocations on an already-migrated legacy auth source
(auth-profiles.json, auth-state.json, auth.json, shared oauth.json) minted a
fresh timestamped .migrated-* archive every run, so prod accumulated ~2.5
snapshots per agent.

When a terminal migration receipt already owns the exact source bytes and its
archive still exists, doctor now removes the reappeared identical source
without creating a new snapshot; only content that actually changed is
archived again. If the terminal archive is missing, doctor still re-archives
to preserve the bytes.

Fixes #132

Co-authored-by: Migration Agent <agent@daroja.ai>
